-- test_eval_divergent_ported.mdk — the assertions/declarations `medaka check`
-- REJECTS BY DESIGN, split out of test_eval_ported.mdk.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS IS THE ONE FILE IN test/ported/ THAT IS GENUINELY UNTYPECHECKABLE.
-- Do NOT "fix" anything here.  Removing a construct below does not make a test
-- pass — it DELETES the coverage, because the construct IS the test: each one is
-- a shape the interpreter accepts and the type checker rejects, and pinning that
-- divergence is why test/ported/ exists (issue #1445).
--
-- Both cases have the same cause, stated by the compiler's own source:
-- `newtypeDerivers` (compiler/frontend/desugar.mdk) is DELIBERATELY shorter than
-- `dataDerivers` — "`Generic` (and `Num`) go through specialized newtype derivers
-- in lib/desugar.ml that this port has not taken, so a newtype genuinely cannot
-- derive them here."  `medaka check` therefore reports
--   cannot derive 'Num' for 'Dist'; supported: Eq, Ord, Debug, Display, Hashable
--   cannot derive 'Generic' for 'WrapGen'; …
-- while `expandDecl` silently DROPS a derive it has no deriver for, the newtype is
-- representationally its payload, and untyped eval's arg-tag dispatch then finds
-- `Num Int` / the `data` Generic impl.  Note the asymmetry that makes this a real
-- divergence and not a typo: `data … deriving (Generic)` IS accepted (see
-- test_eval_ported.mdk's `BoxG`) — only the newtype form is not.
--
-- If `newtypeDerivers` ever grows `Num`/`Generic`, this file's reason to exist
-- ends: check it, and fold it back into test_eval_ported.mdk.
--
-- Ported from: t_newtype_deriving_num_add, t_newtype_deriving_num_mul (the
-- ASSERTIONS for these were already removed 2026-07-11 — newtype constructors are
-- unbound at eval; the declarations remain because they are what diverges).
-- Run with: medaka test test/ported/test_eval_divergent_ported.mdk

import test.{expectEqual}

-- ── newtype deriving (Num) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
newtype Dist = Dist Int deriving (Eq, Num)
distR : Dist
distR = add (Dist 3) (Dist 4)
distRN = match distR
  Dist n => n

distMul : Dist
distMul = mul (Dist 3) (Dist 4)
distMulN = match distMul
  Dist n => n

-- ── newtype deriving (Generic) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Expected shape: RCon "WrapGen" [RInt 5]
newtype WrapGen = WrapGen Int deriving (Generic)
genNewtypeName = match to_rep (WrapGen 5)
  RCon name _ => name
  _ => ""

-- A live assertion so this file is not silently vacuous under `medaka test`.
-- It exercises nothing divergent on its own; the divergence is the declarations
-- above being reached at all.
test "divergent corpus is reached" = expectEqual 1 (1 : Int)
